<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Clermont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1095">1095</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Clermont was a church council held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a> at Clermont in Auvergne in November 1095. Besides decrees on church reform, it ended with Urban's sermon of 27 November calling on western Christians to aid the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, which launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>. The crowd is said to have answered with the cry 'Deus vult' ('God wills it').</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-clermont.jpg" alt="Council of Clermont" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Colombe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Passages_d%27outremer_Fr5594,_fol._19r,_Concile_de_Clermont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
